      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the minced beef with the lemongrass, garlic, shallots, fish sauce, sugar, sesame oil, and ground peanuts. Combine well. Chill for 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Lay a betel leaf flat, shiny side down. Place a tablespoon of beef mixture in a log shape at the base of the leaf. Roll up tightly. Thread onto a skewer through the seam to hold it closed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue until all the beef mixture is used. You should get about 20 rolls."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat a griddle pan to high. Brush the rolls lightly with oil. Grill for 2 to 3 minutes per side until the leaves are charred and the beef is cooked through."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the dipping sauce by combining the fish sauce, lime juice, sugar, and 3 tbsp of water. Add minced garlic and chilli if you like."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Serve the rolls with cooked vermicelli, fresh mint, and coriander. Dip into the sauce before eating."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The rolls unravel on the grill.",
              "cause": "The skewer was not placed through the seam.",
              "fix": "Thread the skewer through the seam of the leaf when it is tightly rolled. This holds the shape and makes turning easier."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The beef is dry inside.",
              "cause": "The rolls were cooked for too long on the grill.",
              "fix": "The rolls need only 2 to 3 minutes per side. The beef inside is thin and cooks quickly. Remove as soon as the leaf chars."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The leaf burns before the beef is cooked.",
              "cause": "The heat was too high or the leaves were too small.",
              "fix": "Use large betel leaves and keep the heat at medium-high rather than maximum. A little charring is desirable but burnt leaves taste bitter."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bò nướng lá lốt is popular across Vietnam but especially loved in the south. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is part of the famous "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "bo-7-mon"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "bò 7 món "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "seven-course beef banquet. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Street vendors grill the rolls to order over charcoal, filling the street with their fragrant smoke. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The dish is also common at garden parties and outdoor barbecues in Vietnam. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Betel leaf has been used in Vietnamese and Southeast Asian cooking for thousands of years."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
